   \{F\}<\^{}>N\$\$\textbackslash{}end\{document\}. One of their key
   applications is to augment general-purpose SNARKs, making them more
   efficient on subcomputations that are hard to arithmetize. In order for
   this ``augmentation{''} to work out, a SNARK and a lookup argument
   should have some basic level of compatibility with respect to the
