   HERCEG, MAR 19-21, 2025},
Abstract = {Each new silicon process VLSI node brings significant changes to the
   RTL-to-GDSII Tcl backend flow, often requiring the manual rewriting of
   ASIC digital Tcl scripts from scratch. In this paper, we review the
   Hammer RTL-to-GDSII flow, a modular platform designed to reduce
   redundant efforts in writing new Tcl scripts when designers switch
   technology nodes or change EDA tool vendors. We highlight the key
   strengths of this flow and identify areas for improvement.},
