Title = {VMS: Visual Cache Memory Simulator with Spatio-Temporal Visualization},
Booktitle = {WORKSHOP ON COMPUTER ARCHITECTURE EDUCATION, WCAE 2025},
Year = {2025},
Note = {2025 Workshop on Computer Architecture Education-WCAE, JAPAN, JUN 21,
   2025},
Abstract = {Understanding how computer programs interact with memory caches is key
   to optimizing system performance. Our paper introduces the Visual Memory
   Simulator (VMS), a user-friendly tool that visualizes caches' temporal
   and spatial utilization. VMS has three components: cache simulator,
   visualization backend, and GUI. It inputs either a C program or a memory
   trace. VMS also provides a tracer so users can generate their memory
   traces.
   VMS is useful for students to understand cache concepts and researchers
   to identify memory bottlenecks. VMS provides an intuitive interface
   where researchers can input code or traces and instantly see cache
   utilization. Dynamic visualizations help identify optimization
   possibilities by showing how programs interact with the cache hierarchy.
   Moreover, VMS allows exploring cache behavior in different settings,
   giving researchers insight into the effects of various configurations
   and access patterns.},
