Abstract = {The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Ambient Intelligence
   (AmI) has emerged as a promising approach to creating responsive and
   contextually aware environments. AmI creates contextually aware
   environments by seamlessly integrating intelligent technologies, while
   AI develops algorithms for autonomous learning and decision-making.
   However, embedding AI within AmI environments faces challenges due to
   limited resources and energy constraints. While recent research on
   embedded AI has primarily focused on specific tasks of AmI, our goal is
   to develop a comprehensive framework encompassing all the necessary
   components for practical use cases. Through this endeavor, we aim to
   explore power-aware designs and distributed learning as fundamental
   approaches to address limited computational resources, energy
   constraints, and dynamic context variations challenges.},
