Abstract = {The rapid advancement of AI (from foundational machine learning to Large
   Language Models) and edge computing has placed unprecedented demands on
   computation, memory, and storage on resource-constrained edge devices.
   As AI models scale, the ability to efficiently manage computing
   resources, utilize memory and storage, and reduce energy consumption has
   become critical. This paper introduces contributions on 4 topics related
   to deploying AI on resource-constrained edge devices: 1) unlocking
   training of foundational machine learning algorithms on the edge, 2)
   exploring hardware-aware DNN architecture and mapping co-optimization
   for inference on heterogeneous systems, 3) scaling RAG by leveraging
   advanced memory, storage, and energy-efficient designs, and 4)
   investigating cost-effective and high-performance large-scale graph
   processing.},
