Year = {2025},
Note = {43rd VLSI Test Symposium-VTS, Tempe, AZ, APR 28-30, 2025},
Abstract = {Evaluating the reliability of deep neural network (DNN) applications is
   essential to assess efficient error resilience techniques and deploy
   artificial intelligence (AI) on safety-critical embedded systems. This
   work presents a novel methodology for assessing the reliability of DNN
   models deployed on microcontrollers using software-level fault
   injection. A new tool was developed, on top of the TensorFlow Lite
   library for C/C++, to inject faults into memory and CPU registers during
   DNN inference. Providing a portable, fast, and configurable approach for
   injecting multiple fault types. The proposed framework was validated
   with two case studies, using a variety of literature-endorsed models and
   datasets, the results provide a comparative analysis of DNN reliability
   versus register and memory bit flips, induced by transient faults.},
