   COMMUNICATION TECHNOLOGIES, CONECCT},
Series = {IEEE International Conference on Electronics Computing and Communication
   Technologies},
Year = {2025},
Note = {11th International Conference on Electronics Computing and Communication
   Technologies-CONECCT-Annual, INDIA, JUL 10-13, 2025},
Abstract = {This work introduces a SecRISC-DFI(Secure RISC-V - Data-Flow Integrity),
   a secure RISC-V design with dynamic information flow tracking to
   implement real-time DFI in the field. The system uses a high-speed DFI
   verification model and Circular Dilated Convolutional Network (CiDi-CN)
   to have improved threat detection. Additionally, Pied Kingfisher
   Optimization (PiKiO) optimizes CiDi-CN parameters to achieve improved
   performance. The design has improved performance with 99.87\% DFI
   violation detection accuracy, 99.42\% system throughput preservation,
   99.16\% false positive reduction rate, and 99.23\% real-time execution
   efficiency. SecRISC-DFI ensures robust security without or with
   negligible performance loss and it establishes a trade-off between
   richness of high-performance computing platform robust for newer RISC-V
   architectures.},
