Note = {11th International Conference on Electronics Computing and Communication
   Technologies-CONECCT-Annual, INDIA, JUL 10-13, 2025},
Abstract = {Side channel attacks pose a security threat to aerospace and unmanned
   aerial vehicles (UAVs), especially in defense scenarios where ensuring
   resilience and safeguarding data confidentiality is of utmost
   importance. These attacks take advantage of information leaks like power
   usage patterns, electromagnetic emissions, timing fluctuations, and
   sound signals to steal cryptographic keys and sensor data or control
   instructions. Due to the increasing complexity of these attacks, it is
   crucial to assess the current mitigation methods to find effective
   defense tactics and steer future research in the right direction. This
   survey consolidates and analyzes diverse strategies to enhance security
   measures such as encryption safeguards, hardwarebased protections,
   obscuring software code, AI-powered anomaly detection, and shielding
   signals. In this study, the balance among security needs, computational
   performance, and system limitations is provided by highlighting a review
   of current options. Furthermore, we highlight research obstacles and
   upcoming paths like quantum-proof encryption methods, advanced
   artificial intelligence-powered intrusion detection, and innovative
   protective measures to strengthen the durability of future aerospace and
   UAV defense systems against new side channel risks. By amalgamating
   existing progress, this analysis offers valuable perspective for
   researchers, technicians, and decision-makers striving to create
   stronger security infrastructures.},
