Note = {2025 Space Aerospace and Defence Conference-SPACE, Bengaluru, INDIA, JUL
   21-23, 2025},
Abstract = {The rover project named Project Makardhwaj is a Martian rover designed
   to be deployed on the Martian surface in a scenario where the human
   explorers are already on the surface and are using rovers as an
   extension for their research, expedition, and discovery. Control plays
   an important role in the progress of any space project. The introduced
   rover control design discovers the ways of implementing a transposable
   and extensible control architecture and still keeping it user accessible
   with improved efficiency. It makes use of the Robot Operating System
   (ROS2) framework for achieving its goal of modular control design. The
   idea of segmented control not only makes debugging easy but also helps
   increase the simplicity of the integration of new functionalities and
   features. It explores the benefits of ROS2 QoS parameters and its
   advantages over the conventional methods. By leveraging ROS2, the
   introduced rover control architecture makes way for innovative and
   efficient robotic collaboration in human-led space exploration, for
   better scientific outcomes and operational flexibility.},
