Note = {6th International Conference on Automation of Software Test-AST-Annual,
   Ottawa, CANADA, APR 28-29, 2025},
Abstract = {Integration testing is a fundamental step of the software development
   process. Due to the high costs, testers may like to automatically
   generate the test cases, but unfortunately current test generators are
   designed for unit testing or system testing, while they are generally
   ill-suited for integration testing. In this paper, we discuss the
   challenges of generating test cases for integration testing, and the
   limitations of current test generators thereby. We elaborate on a novel
   approach to automatically generating test cases for integration testing,
   and report initial evidence in support of our approach.},
