Note = {2025 International Symposium of Electronics Design Automation-ISEDA,
   Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 09-12, 2025},
Abstract = {Vertical interconnects (VI) such as through silicon vias (TSVs),
   micro-solder bumps (mu bumps), and controlled collapse chip connection
   (C4) bumps are critical for accurate thermal modeling in 3D IC. However,
   it has a high complexity to model such VI in thermal simulation.
   Therefore, it is necessary to develop efficient macromodels for
   early-stage planning, physical design, and quick verification. This
   paper develops an efficient yet accurate thermal model for 3D
   integration. We first map layers, which contain TSVs, mu bumps and/or C4
   bumps, to effective layers with homogeneous effective thermal
   conductivity. Moreover, we build a lookup table (LUT) of this
   conductivity for each type of effective layer separately, and show that
   these effective layers can be stacked to compute temperatures in 3D
   integration. Since effective layers with homogeneous conductivity can
   use sparse grids, temperature calculation using field solvers such as
   COMSOL is accelerated significantly. The experimental results show that
   our proposed macromodels achieve 60x speedup compared to the golden
   model simulated with COMSOL (from 30 minutes by COMSOL down to 30
   seconds by our model). Furthermore, existing macromodel studies exhibit
   up to 5.71\% error, whereas our model only has an error of 0.85\% for
   maximum, minimum and mean temperatures. To the best of our knowledge,
   this paper is the first in-depth study on the layerwise thermal
   macromodel for 3D integration with consideration of inter-die layers.},
